  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The equation of electric field is given in the question,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>500</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;now compare it the equation of electric field in an electromagnetic wave,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, so the velocity of electromagnetic waves is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>.</p>",
